    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "66144f62_c4984e93",
        "filename": "android/visibility.go",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 141,
      "author": {
        "id": 1373864
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-04-01T19:12:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I suggest introducing a separate //visibility:legacy_public to use as default. That to make migration to more restrictive visibilities easier: At some point the default can change to //visibility:private while a machine refactoring tool adds //visibility:legacy_public to all rules. Then packages can be gradually converted to better explicit visibility settings, and we can tell the difference between public (\u003d intentionally made public) and legacy_public (\u003d no conscious decision on visibility).\n\n(This is under the premise that we aim to move away from public visibility by default, which I think is a good goal.)",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 141,
        "startChar": 61,
        "endLine": 141,
        "endChar": 72
      },
      "revId": "e084826e95eaf4bfac9f604d4e3f400395cd93d9",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e3fc92b0_a2dfd385",
        "filename": "android/visibility.go",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 141,
      "author": {
        "id": 1039338
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-04-02T13:45:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t see the point in adding legacy_public now. It provides no advantage over simply not specifying the visibility property altogether. I definitely agree that defaulting to private is better though. We can easily add legacy_public later once everything has been switched to soong. Doing it any earlier would just make the conversion to soong more difficult.",
      "parentUuid": "66144f62_c4984e93",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 141,
        "startChar": 61,
        "endLine": 141,
        "endChar": 72
      },
      "revId": "e084826e95eaf4bfac9f604d4e3f400395cd93d9",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "53a225d4_b7190def",
        "filename": "android/visibility.go",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 141,
      "author": {
        "id": 1373864
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-04-02T14:11:47Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The reason to do it now is that it makes the purpose of //visibility:public clear. It can e.g. encourage users to specify //visibility:public explicitly early on, instead of relying on the default.\n\n\u003e Doing it any earlier would just make the conversion to soong more difficult.\n\nIn what way? (Note that I don\u0027t advocate doing the refactoring step at any particular time.)",
      "parentUuid": "e3fc92b0_a2dfd385",
